1
00:00:04,368 --> 00:00:06,848
(Sheldon:)President Seibert, I don't
know why you're yelling.

2
00:00:07,004 --> 00:00:09,214
(Sheldon:)You're the one who
made me go on the radio.

3
00:00:09,373 --> 00:00:12,043
(Sheldon:)I was expecting a professional
science interview,

4
00:00:12,209 --> 00:00:15,559
(Sheldon:)not an attack by some
morning zoo shock jock.

5
00:00:17,515 --> 00:00:19,255
(Sheldon:)Well, if the university
needs money so badly,

6
00:00:19,417 --> 00:00:21,487
(Sheldon:)perhaps you should
start a swear jar.

7
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:25,430
Whoa! That one's worth a dollar.

8
00:00:27,858 --> 00:00:29,098
(Amy:)I know you don't like it,

9
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:30,430
(Amy:)but every time
you do an interview,

10
00:00:30,594 --> 00:00:32,434
(Amy:)it raises the profile
of the university.

11
00:00:32,596 --> 00:00:34,096
(Amy:)That translates to funding.

12
00:00:34,265 --> 00:00:35,105
(Sheldon:)Yeah, well, I'm not just

13
00:00:35,266 --> 00:00:37,436
(Sheldon:)some trained monkey
dancing for coins.

14
00:00:39,103 --> 00:00:40,083
(Leonard:)Of course you're not.

15
00:00:40,237 --> 00:00:41,717
(Leonard:)People love trained monkeys.

16
00:00:44,208 --> 00:00:45,378
(Penny:)How can you not be happy?

17
00:00:45,543 --> 00:00:47,083
(Penny:)You're tall, thin and famous.

18
00:00:47,244 --> 00:00:49,224
(Penny:)Oh, my God,
I'm jealous of Sheldon.

19
00:00:51,382 --> 00:00:53,052
Lock, you're going to be
doing this stuff for a while.

20
00:00:53,217 --> 00:00:55,427
You're just going to have to find
a way to get used to it.

21
00:00:55,586 --> 00:00:57,296
(Sheldon:)But none of you know
what this is like.

22
00:00:57,455 --> 00:01:00,455
(Sheldon:)Being celebrated for something
you wish you never did.

23
00:01:00,624 --> 00:01:07,024
(Penny:)You clearly haven't been with me
at Mardi Gras.

